<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43996" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sesquĭ-pēs</span></b> ,
			pĕdis, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a foot and a half</i> (in length,
			breadth, etc.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cytisum in sesquipedem ponere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 43</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plus quam sesquipedem prohibeat infodere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 13, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Arb. 1, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sesquipede est quam tu longior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Trin. 4, 2, 58</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 8, 60, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Pers. 1,
			57</span></i>.</div>
